From: Ale <345759907+ale-wastedtimeonpc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] accel/amdxdna: aie2: wait for SMU idle before issuing a command

On a Ryzen 9 PRO 8945HS (Hawk Point, npu1 / aie2) the in-tree amdxdna 0.7.0
driver occasionally logs "smu cmd 6 timed out" during runtime resume, when the
DPM H-clock is changed. The amd/xdna-driver main branch avoids this by waiting
for the SMU to finish the previous command (bit 1 of SMU_INTR_REG) before
writing a new one, and by not clearing SMU_INTR_REG before the kick.

This is a test backport of that wait to the in-tree aie2_smu.c only.
Tested with 4,253 forced runtime resumes in 2 hours: 0 SMU timeouts
(before: 1 in 40 and 1 in 643). Details: amd/xdna-driver#1805.

Not an official AMD patch. Use at your own risk.
---
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_smu.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_smu.c
@@ -32,15 +32,26 @@
 static int aie2_smu_exec(struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev, u32 reg_cmd,
 			 u32 reg_arg, u32 *out)
 {
-	u32 resp;
+	u32 resp, intr;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Wait until the SMU has finished the previous command (bit 1 of
+	 * SMU_INTR_REG) before writing a new one, as amd/xdna-driver main does
+	 * in aie_smu_exec() for npu1 (smu_intr_enabled). Test backport only.
+	 */
+	ret = readx_poll_timeout(readl, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_INTR_REG), intr,
+				 !(intr & 0x2), AIE2_INTERVAL, AIE2_TIMEOUT);
+	if (ret) {
+		XDNA_ERR(ndev->xdna, "wait for smu intr idle timed out: 0x%x", intr);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	writel(0, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_RESP_REG));
 	writel(reg_arg, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_ARG_REG));
 	writel(reg_cmd, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_CMD_REG));
 
-	/* Clear and set SMU_INTR_REG to kick off */
-	writel(0, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_INTR_REG));
+	/* Set SMU_INTR_REG to kick off (no clear first, as in main) */
 	writel(1, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_INTR_REG));
 
 	ret = readx_poll_timeout(readl, SMU_REG(ndev, SMU_RESP_REG), resp,
